  "notes": "osunlp/LlaSMol-Mistral-7B = LoRA adapter (modules_to_save=[]) on openly-available mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1, instruction-tuned on SMolInstruct; merged and run with LlaSMol's own PP generation config (num_beams=4, 1 return seq, max_new_tokens=20, deterministic). Prompts are SMolInstruct's EXACT verbatim templates with <SMILES> core tags, SMILES canonicalized by LlaSMol's own canonicalize_molecule_smiles, chat wrapped as <s>[INST] .. [/INST], answers extracted with the repo's TASK_TAGS. Classification ROC-AUC headline = P(Yes) via sequence-LL of the two canonical <BOOLEAN> responses (suite-comparable); LlaSMol-native hard-label AUC/accuracy (calculate_boolean_metrics, verbatim) also reported. clintox evaluated against the CT_TOX endpoint ('Is X toxic?', verified 16/16). sider = mean AUC over the 20/27 endpoints SMolInstruct has templates for (7 masked). Regression RMSE headline imputes the train-target mean for unparseable outputs (over all test molecules); native RMSE (drops unparseable) + count also reported. WARNING: LlaSMol was instruction-tuned on these MoleculeNet PP datasets, and 74-92% of our scaffold-split TEST molecules appear in SMolInstruct's train/dev -- these numbers are NOT held-out generalization."
}